  "reviewed_properties": [
    "The host issues data-use-assessment/1 only for an exact owned successful compilation and its intact dependency versions. Generic sources and workers cannot mint the reserved namespace or call the operator operations.",
    "Prior knowledge starts at the original formalization and traverses source references, exposure, worker context and job bindings. Later compiler-added dependencies are not automatically mislabeled prior LLM knowledge; target IDs already in the original ancestry are never subtracted.",
    "Required missing sources are integrity gaps. Opaque exposure annotations remain unresolved; the limited exploratory pass neither erases them nor claims clean holdout.",
    "Protected assessment/calibration ancestry and unsupported operations ancestry retain gaps for this implemented scope. Host-owned typed implementation packages/certificates are separately reported as technical provenance, and their ancestors are still traversed.",
    "Provider document descriptors, owned blobs, exact hashes, URLs and full original receipt validation are retained. Exact reviewed README and terms pins, rather than free rights prose, constrain personal non-production research use.",
    "The assumed delay is checked against the exact normalizer binding and feature-definition parameters and availability meaning. Historical publication and vintage remain unknown.",
    "Historical plan child output and its raw gate list remain unchanged. Optional data-use evidence is retained in the immutable input capsule and outer record; the current view removes only the scoped data/exposure gate and explicitly returns protected_target_admission=false.",
    "Same-key historical retrieval preserves immutable records. Current use rechecks checker currency, exact findings and typed technical revocation. A changed prerequisite during plan preparation prevents commitment.",
    "An unreadable or changed installed checker fails closed. All scientific readiness, allocation and freeze flags remain false."
  ],
